Drop any extra root certificates (*.crt, PEM format) into this directory and they are
installed into the build containers before NuGet restore runs.

This is only needed behind a TLS-intercepting proxy, where the public NuGet feed presents a
certificate signed by an internal CA that the .NET SDK image does not trust; the symptom is
NU1301 "The remote certificate is invalid because of errors in the certificate chain:
UntrustedRoot". Leave the directory empty on a normal network.

Certificates are deliberately not committed: they are specific to one network.
